<title>USA: Caldwell, N.J., approves $6.6 mln school GO bonds.</title>
<headline>Caldwell, N.J., approves $6.6 mln school GO bonds.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Voters in Caldwell, N.J., on Tuesday approved a $6.6 million school bond issue, a school official said Wednesday.</p>
<p>The vote was 774 in favor and 353 against.</p>
<p>The bonds will be used for new technology, science labs, and building renovations.</p>
<p>--Steven Dickson, 212-859-1652</p>
